//
// Conduit (--use-conduit) end-to-end run for the JOIN last-slice
// BD-length overflow pattern.  The fix has been applied in this working
// tree (ConduitToDMALink.cpp:574-595 — derive joinDstPerBufForLen from
// the JOIN buffer's MemRefType element count instead of the shim
// consumer's per-dispatch num_elems).
//
// PASS expectation: dispatch completes and output bytes match the
// stateful reference computed by test.cpp.
//
// Pre-fix behavior (kept here for context, NOT the current state of the
// tree): Pass C emits dma_bd len = 448 against memref<128xbf16> memtile
// JOIN buffers (4× overflow).  The cross-buffer write hangs firmware
// and the dispatch never returns a completion token; the host wait would
// TIMEOUT (this lit would be a hang/timeout, not a wrong-bytes mismatch).
//
// npu2 only: this is the LM-head GEMM target where the bug surfaces in
// Llama; npu1's per-channel pool / BD topology is not the regression
// surface for this fix.
//
// NOTE: this lit is intentionally NOT marked XFAIL.  If the post-fix
// build hangs or fails on hardware, that is a real signal that the fix
// needs further work — DO NOT silence by adding XFAIL.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai
//
// RUN: cp %S/aie.mlir aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu2_1col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %python aiecc.py --no-aiesim --aie-generate-xclbin --aie-generate-npu-insts --no-compile-host --use-conduit --xclbin-name=aie.xclbin --npu-insts-name=insts.bin aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: clang %S/test.cpp -o test.exe -std=c++17 -Wall %xrt_flags -lrt -lstdc++ %test_utils_flags
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE -i insts.bin
